BIT/EV of 3.5% (vs the 8% bar).","The 24 covering analysts target $208 on average, 13% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 32% clears the cost of capital of 8.6% by 24pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.44).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 1.80x, but high accruals (-9.1% of assets).","ROE of 28% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.4x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.8% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","The current ratio of 0.50 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 13.5% over 3 years, 19.6% over 5 years and 12.5% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating.","At current returns, reinvesting 9% of profits supports about 2.8% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 35.1% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 12%.","Capex runs 1.9x depreciation (6.6% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 25, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.4%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (12 sales, net $5.3M sold).","It returns 2.7% a year to shareholders (1.2% in buybacks and 1.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 15 consecutive years, raising it 48.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 101,000 employees, each generates about $58K of revenue, 0.2x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 12.6% a year.","That works out to $3K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.4M (41x revenue per employee)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":61,"head":"Avoid: priced 42% above its fair value of $129.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 57, gates 13/26)","ROIC 32.3% vs WACC 8.6%","Revenue grew 19.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.2x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 42% above fair value of $129","P/E 28.9x vs sector 19.3x","EV/EBITDA 18.7x vs sector 11.2x","P/FCF 35.3x vs sector 16.5x"],"flags":["Priced 42% above its fair value of $129"],"need":[],"buy_below":109.8,"vc":{"base":129.18,"base_src":"dcf","bear":98.79,"bull":173.94,"alt_median":77.99,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.6563,"dispersion":0.1887,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 66% above the other models' median ($77.99)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"TXRH","date":"2026-11-06"}